{"name":"Elemental","hex":"#d0d3d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elemental","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or being an element (as opposed to a compound).","Basic, fundamental or elementary."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A creature (usually a spirit) that is attuned with, or composed of, one of the classical elements: air, earth, fire and water or variations of them like ice, lightning, etc. They sometimes have unique proper names and sometimes are referred to as Air, Earth, Fire, or Water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elemental"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elemental","blocks":[{"text":"An elemental is a mythic supernatural being that is described in occult and alchemical works from around the time of the European Renaissance, and particularly elaborated in the 16th century works of Paracelsus. According to Paracelsus and his subsequent followers, there are four categories of elementals, which are gnomes, undines, sylphs, and salamanders. These correspond to the four Empedoclean elements of antiquity: earth, water, air, and fire, respectively. Terms employed for beings associated with alchemical elements vary by source and gloss."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Undine_Rising_from_the_Waters%2C_front.JPG/330px-Undine_Rising_from_the_Waters%2C_front.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elemental"},{"title":"Elemental (2023 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Elemental is a 2023 American animated romantic comedy-drama film directed by Peter Sohn, and written by John Hoberg, Kat Likkel, and Brenda Hsueh. Produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures, it stars the voices of Leah Lewis, Mamoudou Athie, Ronnie del Carmen, Shila Ommi, Wendi McLendon-Covey, and Catherine O'Hara. Set in a world inhabited by anthropomorphic elements of nature, the story follows fire element Ember Lumen (Lewis) and water element Wade Ripple (Athie), who spend time together in the city while trying to save a convenience store owned by Ember's father, Bernie."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Elemental_final_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elemental_(2023_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/The_Elements%2C_Chelsea_Porcelain_Manufactory_-_Indianapolis_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC00573.JPG/500px-The_Elements%2C_Chelsea_Porcelain_Manufactory_-_Indianapolis_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC00573.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/The_Elements%2C_Chelsea_Porcelain_Manufactory_-_Indianapolis_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC00573.JPG/1280px-The_Elements%2C_Chelsea_Porcelain_Manufactory_-_Indianapolis_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC00573.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/The_Elements%2C_Chelsea_Porcelain_Manufactory_-_Indianapolis_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC00573.JPG/500px-The_Elements%2C_Chelsea_Porcelain_Manufactory_-_Indianapolis_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC00573.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rococo set of personification figurines of the Four Elements, 1760s, Chelsea porcelain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Elements%2C_Chelsea_Porcelain_Manufactory_-_Indianapolis_Museum_of_Art_-_DSC00573.JPG"}],"sounds":{"elemental":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-elemental.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-elemental.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame